# GenSpark UI Design System Rules

You are developing for GenSpark project. Follow these UI design system rules strictly:

## Color System

### Color Variables (Always Use)
```css
/* ===== 主色系统 ===== */
--color-primary: #232425;              /* 品牌黑色主色 - 用于按钮、文字、主要操作等 */
--color-primary-hover: #393A3B;        /* 主色悬停态 */

/* ===== 品牌蓝色系统（强引导/特殊功能） ===== */
--color-brand-blue: #0F7FFF;           /* 品牌蓝色 - 用于强引导、转化点、特殊功能 */
--color-brand-blue-hover: #0E72E5;     /* 品牌蓝色悬停态 */

/* ===== 品牌色应用延展 ===== */
--color-brand-darkest: #031933;        /* 品牌色最深 */
--color-brand-darker: #063366;         /* 品牌色深 */
--color-brand-dark: #094C99;           /* 品牌色中深 */
--color-brand-medium: #0C66CC;         /* 品牌色中等 - 外链类型使用 */
--color-brand-primary: #0F7FFF;        /* 品牌色主色 */
--color-brand-light: #3F99FF;          /* 品牌色浅 */
--color-brand-lighter: #9FCCFF;        /* 品牌色更浅 */
--color-brand-lightest: #CFE5FF;       /* 品牌色最浅 */
--color-brand-pale: #F3F9FF;           /* 品牌色极浅 */

/* ===== 文本超链接 ===== */
--color-link: #0C66CC;                 /* 文本超链接等可点内文 */

/* ===== 品牌色/主色 ===== */
--color-brand-black: #232425;          /* 品牌黑色（主色） */

/* ===== 品牌色/频道色 ===== */
--color-channel-travel: #5CD4A1;       /* Travel 频道色 */
--color-channel-product: #73A0F8;      /* Product 频道色 */
--color-channel-product-alt: #8B62E2;  /* Product 频道色（紫色） */
--color-channel-fashion: #232425;      /* Fashion 频道色 */
--color-channel-finance: #73D2F8;      /* Finance 频道色 */

/* ===== 功能色 ===== */
--color-success: #5CD4A1;              /* 界面功能正向反馈用色 */
--color-success-alt: #58D464;          /* 图片示意中的颜色 */

/* ===== 警示色/重要提示 ===== */
--color-danger: #FF3D3D;               /* 错误/危险色 */
--color-warning-light: #FF7C7C;        /* 警告色（浅） */
--color-warning: #FFC107;              /* 异常状态要提醒 */

/* ===== 文本色系统 ===== */
--color-text-primary: #232425;         /* 正文主标题，列表标题等重要信息 */
--color-text-secondary: #606366;       /* 正文,等主要文本 */
--color-text-tertiary: #909499;        /* 辅助信息文字，输入框默认提示字色 */
--color-text-quaternary: #CCCCCC;      /* 辅助信息文字，输入框默认提示字色（更浅） */

/* ===== 背景色系统 ===== */
--color-bg-primary: #E5E5E5;           /* 常规列表页 次要功能界面（背景色） */
--color-bg-secondary: #F5F5F5;         /* 常规列表页 次要功能界面（背景色） */
--color-bg-tertiary: #FAFAFA;          /* 内文的底色等弱背景色 */
--color-bg-functional: #EFEFEF;        /* 功能性文字背景 */

/* ===== 分割线色系统 ===== */
--color-divider-dark: #EAEAEA;         /* 列表分割线（适配深色） */
--color-divider-light: #EFEFEF;        /* 列表分割线（适配浅色） */
--color-divider-special: #D9D9D9;      /* 线框按钮（特别） */

/* ===== 彩色辅助系统 ===== */
--color-auxiliary-cyan: #C4F4FF;       /* 辅助色-青色 */
--color-auxiliary-amber: #FFEBC4;      /* 辅助色-琥珀色 */
--color-auxiliary-green: #C4FFD1;      /* 辅助色-绿色 */
--color-auxiliary-red: #FFC4C4;        /* 辅助色-红色 */
--color-auxiliary-purple: #E4DDFF;     /* 辅助色-紫色 */

/* ===== 兼容性颜色（保持向后兼容） ===== */
--color-guide: #0F7FFF;                /* 引导按钮色（品牌蓝色） */
--color-guide-hover: #0E72E5;          /* 引导按钮悬停色 */
--color-secondary: #F5F5F5;            /* 次要按钮背景色 */
--color-secondary-hover: #E9E9E9;      /* 次要按钮悬停色 */
--color-border: #E2E2E2;               /* 边框色 */
```

### Color Usage Rules
**CRITICAL**: Follow these color usage rules strictly:

#### Primary Colors Usage
- **Brand Black (#232425)**: PRIMARY color for buttons, text, main actions and important information
- **Brand Blue (#0F7FFF)**: ONLY for strong guidance, conversion points, special functions and feature highlights
- **Link Color (#0C66CC)**: ONLY for external links and clickable text content

#### Text Color Hierarchy
1. **Primary Text (#232425)**: Main titles, list titles, important information
2. **Secondary Text (#606366)**: Body text, main content
3. **Tertiary Text (#909499)**: Helper text, input placeholders
4. **Quaternary Text (#CCCCCC)**: Disabled text, very light helper text

#### Background Color System
1. **Primary Background (#E5E5E5)**: Regular list pages, secondary functional interfaces
2. **Secondary Background (#F5F5F5)**: Regular list pages, secondary functional interfaces
3. **Tertiary Background (#FAFAFA)**: Content backgrounds, weak background colors
4. **Functional Background (#EFEFEF)**: Functional text backgrounds

#### Brand Blue Usage (Use Sparingly)
**ONLY use Brand Blue (#0F7FFF) for:**
- Strong feature guidance and onboarding
- Conversion-focused call-to-action buttons
- Special promotional features
- Key feature highlights
- Important notifications that require immediate attention

**DO NOT use Brand Blue for:**
- Regular form submissions
- Standard navigation
- Common UI interactions
- Secondary actions

#### Channel Colors (Use Sparingly)
- **Travel**: #5CD4A1 (Green)
- **Product**: #73A0F8 (Blue) or #8B62E2 (Purple)
- **Fashion**: #232425 (Black)
- **Finance**: #73D2F8 (Light Blue)

#### Functional Colors
- **Success**: #5CD4A1 (Interface positive feedback)
- **Success Alt**: #58D464 (Image indication color)
- **Danger**: #FF3D3D (Error/danger)
- **Warning Light**: #FF7C7C (Light warning)
- **Warning**: #FFC107 (Abnormal status reminder)

#### Auxiliary Colors (For Special Tags)
- **Cyan**: #C4F4FF
- **Amber**: #FFEBC4
- **Green**: #C4FFD1
- **Red**: #FFC4C4
- **Purple**: #E4DDFF

## Button Design System

### Button Types & Usage

#### Primary Button (Large Radius)
- Use for: Main actions, natural/relaxed operations
- CSS: `background: var(--color-primary); border-radius: 30px; color: white;`
- Hover: `background: var(--color-primary-hover); box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(35, 36, 37, 0.15);`

#### Primary Button (Small Radius) 
- Use for: Function operations, confirmations, serious actions
- CSS: `background: var(--color-primary); border-radius: 8px; color: white;`
- Hover: `background: var(--color-primary-hover); box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(35, 36, 37, 0.15);`

#### Guide Button (Brand Blue) - Strong Guidance
- Use for: Strong feature guidance, conversion points, special functions
- CSS: `background: var(--color-brand-blue); border-radius: 30px; color: white;`
- Hover: `background: var(--color-brand-blue-hover); box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(15, 127, 255, 0.15);`

#### Outline Button
- Use for: Secondary actions, cancel operations
- CSS: `background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 12px; color: var(--color-text-primary);`
- Hover: `background: var(--color-text-primary); color: white;`

#### Secondary Button (Weak)
- Use for: Auxiliary functions, settings, toggles
- CSS: `background: var(--color-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--color-bg-secondary); border-radius: 12px; color: var(--color-text-primary);`
- Hover: `background: var(--color-secondary-hover);`

#### Danger Button
- Use for: Destructive actions, delete operations
- CSS: `background: var(--color-danger); border-radius: 8px; color: white;`
- Hover: `background: #E53535; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(255, 61, 61, 0.15);`

### Button Sizes
- Large: `width: 208px; height: 40px; font-size: 16px;`
- Medium: `width: 144px; height: 36px; font-size: 16px;`
- Small: `width: 96px; height: 28px; font-size: 16px;`

## Modal Design System

### Modal Types & Usage

#### Confirmation Modal
- Use for: Delete confirmations, important decisions
- Size: Small (300-400px width)
- Content: Warning icon, clear message, Cancel + Confirm buttons
- Buttons: Outline (cancel) + Primary-small (confirm/delete)
- **Border Radius Rule**: Both buttons use 8px radius for serious/compact feeling

#### Form Modal
- Use for: Data input, settings, personalization
- Size: Medium (450-600px width)
- Content: Form fields, labels, validation
- Buttons: Outline (cancel) + Primary-large (submit)
- **Border Radius Rule**: Both buttons use 12px radius for functional consistency

#### Notification Modal
- Use for: Alerts, promotions, updates
- Size: Small-Medium (350-500px width)
- Content: Icon, title, description, single action
- Buttons: Primary-large (main action) or Secondary (dismiss)
- **Border Radius Rule**: Both buttons use 12px radius for balanced appearance

#### Preview Modal
- Use for: Image/content preview, detailed views
- Size: Large (600-800px width)
- Content: Media, metadata, actions
- Buttons: Secondary (close) + Optional primary actions
- **Border Radius Rule**: Both buttons use 12px radius for functional consistency

#### Settings Modal
- Use for: Configuration, preferences, complex forms
- Size: Medium-Large (500-700px width)
- Content: Tabs, form sections, advanced options
- Buttons: Outline (cancel) + Primary-small (save)
- **Border Radius Rule**: Both buttons use 12px radius for functional consistency

### Modal Sizes
- Small: `width: 300-400px; max-height: 400px;`
- Medium: `width: 450-600px; max-height: 600px;`
- Large: `width: 600-800px; max-height: 90vh;`

### Modal Structure (Always Use)
```css
.modal-overlay {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0; left: 0;
  width: 100%; height: 100%;
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  z-index: 1000;
  opacity: 0;
  visibility: hidden;
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
}

.modal-dialog {
  background: white;
  border-radius: 16px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
  padding: 24px;
  transform: scale(0.9) translateY(20px);
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
  max-width: 90vw;
  max-height: 90vh;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.modal-overlay.active {
  opacity: 1;
  visibility: visible;
}

.modal-overlay.active .modal-dialog {
  transform: scale(1) translateY(0);
}
```

### Modal Header Pattern
```html
<div class="modal-header">
  <h2 class="modal-title">Title</h2>
  <button class="close-btn" aria-label="Close">×</button>
</div>
```

### Modal Footer Pattern
```html
<!-- Confirmation Modal - Both buttons use 8px radius -->
<div class="modal-footer">
  <button class="btn-base btn-outline-8px btn-medium">Cancel</button>
  <button class="btn-base btn-primary-8px btn-medium">Confirm</button>
</div>

<!-- Form Modal - Both buttons use 12px radius -->
<div class="modal-footer">
  <button class="btn-base btn-outline btn-medium">Cancel</button>
  <button class="btn-base btn-primary-12px btn-medium">Submit</button>
</div>

<!-- Settings Modal - Both buttons use 12px radius -->
<div class="modal-footer">
  <button class="btn-base btn-outline btn-medium">Cancel</button>
  <button class="btn-base btn-primary-12px btn-medium">Save</button>
</div>
```

## Design Rules

### Border Radius Standards
- Large radius (30px): Natural, relaxed - for primary/guide buttons
- Medium radius (16px): Standard - for modals, cards
- Small radius (12px): Functional - for outline/secondary buttons  
- Compact radius (8px): Serious - for functional operations

### Modal Button Border Radius Consistency Rule
**IMPORTANT**: When a modal has two buttons, both buttons MUST use the same border radius for visual consistency:
- **Confirmation modals**: Both buttons use 8px radius (serious/compact feeling)
- **Form modals**: Both buttons use 12px radius (functional consistency)
- **Notification modals**: Both buttons use 12px radius (balanced appearance)
- **Preview modals**: Both buttons use 12px radius (functional consistency)
- **Settings modals**: Both buttons use 12px radius (functional consistency)

### Required Component States
1. Normal: Default appearance
2. Hover: Add box-shadow and color change
3. Disabled: `opacity: 0.3; cursor: not-allowed;`
4. Loading: Show spinner, hide text
5. Focus: Outline for accessibility

### Base Component Classes
```css
.btn-base {
  border: none; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; font-weight: 500;
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  gap: 8px; transition: all 0.25s ease; white-space: nowrap;
  outline: none; box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Button radius variants for modal consistency */
.btn-primary-8px { 
  background: var(--color-primary); 
  color: white; 
  border-radius: 8px; 
}
.btn-primary-8px:hover { 
  background: var(--color-primary-hover); 
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(35, 36, 37, 0.15); 
}

.btn-primary-12px { 
  background: var(--color-primary); 
  color: white; 
  border-radius: 12px; 
}
.btn-primary-12px:hover { 
  background: var(--color-primary-hover); 
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(35, 36, 37, 0.15); 
}

.btn-outline-8px { 
  background: transparent; 
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border); 
  color: var(--color-text-primary); 
  border-radius: 8px; 
}
.btn-outline-8px:hover { 
  background: var(--color-text-primary); 
  color: white; 
}

.btn-outline-12px { 
  background: transparent; 
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border); 
  color: var(--color-text-primary); 
  border-radius: 12px; 
}
.btn-outline-12px:hover { 
  background: var(--color-text-primary); 
  color: white; 
}

.btn-guide-12px { 
  background: var(--color-brand-blue); 
  color: white; 
  border-radius: 12px; 
}
.btn-guide-12px:hover { 
  background: var(--color-brand-blue-hover); 
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(15, 127, 255, 0.15); 
}

.btn-guide-30px { 
  background: var(--color-brand-blue); 
  color: white; 
  border-radius: 30px; 
}
.btn-guide-30px:hover { 
  background: var(--color-brand-blue-hover); 
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(15, 127, 255, 0.15); 
}

.btn-danger-8px { 
  background: var(--color-danger); 
  color: white; 
  border-radius: 8px; 
}
.btn-danger-8px:hover { 
  background: #E53535; 
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(255, 61, 61, 0.15); 
}

.btn-secondary-12px { 
  background: var(--color-secondary); 
  border: 1px solid var(--color-bg-secondary); 
  color: var(--color-text-primary); 
  border-radius: 12px; 
}
.btn-secondary-12px:hover { 
  background: var(--color-secondary-hover); 
}

.modal-base {
  font-family: inherit; 
  color: var(--color-text-primary); 
  line-height: 1.5;
}

/* Text color utilities */
.text-primary { color: var(--color-text-primary); }
.text-secondary { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
.text-tertiary { color: var(--color-text-tertiary); }
.text-quaternary { color: var(--color-text-quaternary); }
.text-link { color: var(--color-link); }
.text-brand { color: var(--color-primary); }
.text-success { color: var(--color-success); }
.text-danger { color: var(--color-danger); }
.text-warning { color: var(--color-warning); }

/* Background color utilities */
.bg-primary { background-color: var(--color-bg-primary); }
.bg-secondary { background-color: var(--color-bg-secondary); }
.bg-tertiary { background-color: var(--color-bg-tertiary); }
.bg-functional { background-color: var(--color-bg-functional); }
```

## Usage Rules

### Modal + Button Combinations
1. **Confirmation Dialogs**: Outline-8px (cancel) + Primary-8px (confirm) - Both use 8px radius
2. **Form Submissions**: Outline-12px (cancel) + Primary-12px (submit) - Both use 12px radius
3. **Feature Guidance**: Outline-12px (skip) + Guide-12px (proceed) - Both use 12px radius
4. **Settings/Preferences**: Outline-12px (cancel) + Primary-12px (save) - Both use 12px radius
5. **Destructive Actions**: Outline-8px (cancel) + Danger-8px (delete) - Both use 8px radius

**CRITICAL RULE**: Both buttons in a modal MUST have the same border radius for visual consistency.

### Accessibility Requirements
1. Modal must trap focus and return to trigger element
2. ESC key closes modal
3. Click outside modal closes it (unless critical)
4. Proper ARIA labels and roles
5. Minimum 44x44px touch targets
6. Color contrast ratio 4.5:1

### Component Hierarchy Rules
1. Only ONE primary button per modal
2. Use guide buttons sparingly for conversion points
3. Maintain clear visual hierarchy
4. Consistent spacing: 16px between sections, 12px between buttons
5. Modal width should not exceed content needs

## React/Vue Component Patterns

### Modal Component Interface
```typescript
interface ModalProps {
  type: 'confirmation' | 'form' | 'notification' | 'preview' | 'settings';
  size: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';
  show: boolean;
  onClose: () => void;
  title: string;
  children: React.ReactNode;
  footer?: React.ReactNode;
  closeOnOutsideClick?: boolean;
  closeOnEsc?: boolean;
}
```

### Button Component Interface
```typescript
interface ButtonProps {
  variant: 'primary-large' | 'primary-small' | 'guide' | 'outline' | 'secondary' | 'danger';
  size: 'large' | 'medium' | 'small';
  disabled?: boolean;
  loading?: boolean;
  icon?: React.ReactNode;
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onClick?: () => void;
}
```

## Code Quality Requirements
- Use CSS custom properties for all colors
- Include all component states (normal, hover, disabled, loading, focus)
- Follow consistent naming: btn-{variant}-{size}, modal-{type}
- Add proper TypeScript interfaces
- Include accessibility attributes (aria-label, role, aria-describedby)
- Implement proper focus management for modals
- Use semantic HTML elements

## Common Modal Patterns

### Delete Confirmation
```html
<div class="modal-overlay active">
  <div class="modal-dialog" style="width: 400px;">
    <div class="modal-header">
      <h2>Confirm Delete</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modal-body">
      <p>This action cannot be undone.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="modal-footer">
      <button class="btn-base btn-outline btn-medium">Cancel</button>
      <button class="btn-base btn-primary-small btn-medium">Delete</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Form Modal
```html
<div class="modal-overlay active">
  <div class="modal-dialog" style="width: 500px;">
    <div class="modal-header">
      <h2>Edit Profile</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modal-body">
      <form><!-- form fields --></form>
    </div>
    <div class="modal-footer">
      <button class="btn-base btn-outline btn-medium">Cancel</button>
      <button class="btn-base btn-primary-large btn-medium">Save Changes</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

IMPORTANT: Never deviate from these specifications. Always use the correct modal type and button combination for the intended use case. Ask for clarification if requirements conflict with these rules.